<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Sultanate of Itsandra</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1886 CE (approx.) · capital Itsandra</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the rival sultanates of Grande Comore, whose rulers long competed with Bambao for the island's paramount title.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grande-comore">Grande Comore</a> (Ngazidja) was divided among several Shirazi-descended lineages from around the 15th century, each ruling a district from a walled stone town. Itsandra, on the west coast north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moroni">Moroni</a>, became one of the most powerful of these by about 1500.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The sultan ruled with the elders of the leading lineages under a matrilineal succession system, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> shaped law and town life. The island's sultans contested the title of sultan tibe, a paramount position over the others, and Itsandra and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-bambao">Sultanate of Bambao</a> were the main rivals. Wealth came from trade with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> coast and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Prolonged wars between the sultanates weakened Itsandra in the 19th century. In 1886 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/said-ali-bin-said-omar">Said Ali of Bambao</a> accepted a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> over the whole island, ending Itsandra's independence. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grande-comore">Grande Comore</a> later became part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comoro-islands">Comoros</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1500 CE – 1886 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.55%;width:7.68%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1886 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Itsandra</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Shingazidja</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Comoros</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Itsandra</dd></dl></aside></div>

